      },
      {
        "amount": "",
        "unit": "",
        "name": "Pickled jalapeños (optional)"
      }
    ],
    "steps": [
      {
        "text": "In a bowl, combine 125 ml milk with 1 tbsp lemon juice and let it stand for 3 minutes to create a quick buttermilk substitute."
      },
      {
        "text": "Add 2 tbsp soy sauce, 1 tbsp honey, 1 tbsp sriracha, 1 tsp garlic paste, 1 tsp ginger paste, and season with salt and pepper. Mix well, then add the 2 chicken breasts and coat evenly. Cover and refrigerate for 1 to 2 hours."
      },
      {
        "text": "Place 2 cups of Kellogg's Frosties into a shallow dish and crush them into small pieces, avoiding a fine powder. In a second shallow dish, whisk together 1 beaten egg and 2 tbsp milk."
      },
      {
        "text": "Remove the chicken from the marinade, allowing any excess to drip off. Dip each chicken breast into the egg mixture, then press firmly into the crushed Frosties until evenly coated on all sides."
      },
      {
        "text": "Preheat an air fryer or Ninja Woodfire Grill using the Air Fry function to 180°C. Lightly spray or oil the basket, place the coated chicken inside, and cook for 12 minutes, flipping halfway through, until the chicken reaches an internal temperature of 75°C."
      },
      {
        "text": "While the chicken cooks, combine 5 tbsp honey, 2 tbsp soy sauce, 1 tbsp sriracha, 1 tsp garlic paste, 1 tsp ginger paste, and 1 tsp sesame oil in a small saucepan. Cook over medium heat, stirring frequently, until the glaze thickens slightly, about 3 to 4 minutes."
      },
      {
        "text": "Brush the hot cooked chicken generously with the warm sweet and spicy glaze, coating all sides."
      },
      {
        "text": "Spread sriracha mayo over both halves of the 2 toasted brioche buns. Add lettuce or slaw to the bottom buns, place the glazed chicken on top, sprinkle with a handful of extra crushed Frosties for added crunch, then add pickled jalapeños if desired. Finish with the top buns and serve immediately."
      }
    ],
    "ninjaSettings": {
      "function": "Air Fry",
      "woodfireFlavor": false,
      "temp": "180",
      "pelletType": "None",
      "probeTarget": "75\u00b0C",
      "doneness": "75°C Internal"
    },
    "notes": "Adjust the amount of sriracha in both the marinade and glaze to suit your preferred spice level. For the crispiest coating, crush the Frosties into small pieces rather than a fine powder. Leftover glazed chicken is excellent sliced into wraps or salads.",
